    "text": "To determine how much the convenience store pays for syrup a week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of syrup boxes needed per week:**\n   The store sells 180 gallons of soda a week, and each syrup box can make 30 gallons of soda. Therefore, the number of syrup boxes needed per week is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{180 \\text{ gallons}}{30 \\text{ gallons/box}} = 6 \\text{ boxes}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total cost of the syrup boxes:**\n   Each syrup box costs $40. Therefore, the total cost for 6 boxes is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\text{ boxes} \\times 40 \\text{ dollars/box} = 240 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the total amount the convenience store pays for syrup a week is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).",
